Justin wrote:
> Probably the best way to get a stolen AoLS back is
> to tame the nymph (scroll of taming or magic harp), and she'll drop
> it.

Not if she's wearing it, according to my reading of the code, and a 
wizmode test. And if she isn't wearing it, killing her will retrieve it. 
  I suppose it could be worth taming her if you can't kill her in a 
single blow. You shouldn't throw stuff, as she'll wear the amulet when 
she picks anything else up. Nymphs have a MR of 20, so taming isn't 
guaranteed.

I don't think taming her then polymorphing her will help too much 
either, except that if you get something buff, you might not mind so 
much it has the AoLS.

The good news is, it looks like there may be a slight loophole; the 
nymph won't wear something she stole until she does an action that will 
trigger the code that checks for stuff to wear. The steal code doesn't 
do that. Until then, she won't wear it. So the best thing to do is 
probably kill her (or possibly tame her) quick.

Things that I can see that will trigger the wearing code are picking 
anything else up or polymorphing, although with luck she might polymorph 
into something that can't put amulets on.

You can tell if she's wearing the AoLS by probing her.

> You can also polymorph into a monster with a steal attack --
> nymph or foocubus -- and smack her to steal it back.  Being in one of
> these forms will also prevent nymphs from stealing from you.

I think this is the only way you'll get back an AoLS once it's worn; the 
monster won't give it up voluntarily.

But who cares? AoLS are optional, and you can always polypile a few if 
you feel you need them for your ascension run.

